oboration therefore exists, and POL-RD-07(iii) and POL-RD-10(3) require ESCALATE rather than a finding in either direction. POL-RD-13 does not alter this: it states in terms that where the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) and no POL-RD-07(ii) corroboration exists, POL-RD-10(3) still governs. Independently, the deciding distance fact is carried only by the 0.6-weight trace, so under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence cannot exceed 0.6, below the 0.70 floor that POL-RD-10(1) enforces. The driver's counterparty statement ('Navigation rerouted me') is evidence and is considered, but it carries no weight_multiplier, cannot lift that cap, and is in any event an uncorroborated assertion about cause rather than a record of the measured route, so it neither corroborates the deviation nor dissolves the escalation. CLAIMS ANSWERED. The driver's asserted external traffic cause is weightless: no traffic_advisory covers this window (EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0) and POL-RD-03 is unavailable. POL-RD-04 does not apply (empty chat log, no rider instruction, no waypoint_hint). POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 do not apply (no amendment timestamps, amended_optimal_distance_km null; vehicle type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL). POL-RD-09 produces nothing to correct on top (tolls_erp 0.00, airport_surcharge 0.00, no gantries). POL-RD-06 is not engaged: the deviation is not material (30.0% below 50%, 4.2 km below 8.0 km) and no pattern exists (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 417 completed_trips_90d), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral. POL-RD-08's rider-side corroboration uplift is not triggered (deviation_claims_60d 0). No profile field decides anything: rating, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld and prior_deviation_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01 and are not relied on. Claims the referee discarded for citing the impaired artifacts without naming their issue codes are recorded in discarded_claims and are not relied on. WHAT WOULD RESOLVE THIS: a complete or repaired trace, or one of the independent sources POL-RD-07(ii) names - a chat-log admission, charged ERP gantries placing the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use, a counterparty statement admitting the measured route, or a platform-derived distance figure that is not a copy of this trace. No referral issues: no clause in this case produces one."
