{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: this dispute goes to a human reviewer. No refund issues now and no further charge is enforced; the $26.73 already charged is held until a person decides (POL-RD-10).\n\nWhat the record shows. The trip ran 18.2 km against a 14.0 km optimal route - an excess of 4.2 km, 30.0% of the optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%), so on the numbers alone a route deviation would be established.\n\nWhy it cannot be decided here. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02850) is impaired. Its weight_multiplier is 0.6 (admissibility issue GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW) and it is also impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a): it carries a 100.0-second gap between consecutive fixes (22:07:31 to 22:09:11), over the 90-second limb. Both things are true and I say both. Where the trace is impaired this way, POL-RD-07(ii) forbids establishing the deviation on the trace alone; it must be corroborated by an independent source. There is none. The chat log (EV-CHAT-02850) is empty, so no rider-requested detour and no driver admission in chat. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02850) carries no ERP gantry lines, so no charged gantry places the vehicle off the optimal corridor. The 18.2 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02850) and on the fare breakdown are copies of the same trace measurement - POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-07(ii) both say so - and are not independent. The driver's statement, 'Navigation rerouted me.', is an assertion of an external cause that names no advisory and no artifact; with no traffic_advisory on file (EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0) POL-RD-13 makes it weightless, and it does not supply the POL-RD-07(ii) corroboration. (The missing advisory is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation, because the driver cited no advisory identifier.)\n\nThe trigger. POL-RD-10(3): the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names exists. POL-RD-07(iii) directs ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the gap is a data failure and not a finding for the driver. POL-RD-10(1) reinforces it: the only artifact carrying the deviation is the 0.6-weight trace, so confidence is capped at 0.6, below the 0.70 floor.\n\nThe remaining claims. The POL-RD-02 arithmetic both sides put forward is correct but cannot issue: charged_total 26.73, recomputed_fare 20.42 = (3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 19.0) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP, refund 6.31, rounded up to 6.35. No relocation (POL-RD-05) and no pooled baseline (POL-RD-12; the vehicle is RYDE_X) apply; no ERP or surcharge correction (POL-RD-09) is due, since the fare carries no gantry lines and no airport surcharge; and no repeat-deviation pattern (POL-RD-06) is established, because the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 417 completed_trips_90d, so there is no conduct referral and no FULL_REFUND uplift. There are no unmatched charge lines, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing referral. The referrals list is empty.\n\nWhat would decide it. A GPS export covering the gap, an ERP gantry record, an independent distance source placing the vehicle on the deviating corridor, or a traffic advisory covering the trip window. A human reviewer can request these under POL-GEN-06."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute cannot be decided on the present record, so it goes to a human reviewer. The amount in dispute (SGD 9.50 of the SGD 26.73 charged for the trip) is held — neither collected nor refunded for now.\n\nThe obstacle is the GPS trace. The platform's pre-check tagged EV-GPS-02850 IMPAIRED, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW, at weight 0.6, because it carries a 100.0-second gap between fixes (22:07:31 to 22:09:11) across which the vehicle covered 1.0 km in a straight line. A gap over 90 seconds also makes the trace impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a). Where the trace is impaired, a deviation cannot be proved from the trace alone; it must be corroborated by an independent source of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) lists, and there is none here. The chat log has 0 messages; the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines; the trip record's 18.2 km and the fare breakdown's billed 18.2 km are copies of the same trace measurement (POL-RD-01), so they corroborate nothing; and the driver's 'Navigation rerouted me' is an explanation of cause, not an admission of the route, and with no traffic advisory on file (EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0) it carries no weight under POL-RD-08 / POL-RD-13. POL-RD-10(3) therefore fires.\n\nIndependently, the fact that would decide this case — that the trip ran 18.2 km against a 14.0 km optimal route, an excess of 4.2 km (30.0%) — is carried by the impaired trace, at weight 0.6, and by nothing independent of it. My confidence is capped at that 0.6, below the platform-wide floor of 0.70, so POL-RD-10(1) also fires.\n\nOn the parties' arguments: both sides' arithmetic for a partial refund is correct as far as it goes — charged_total SGD 26.73; a recomputed fare on the optimal route of SGD 20.42 ((3.80 + 0.75 × 14.0 + 0.28 × 19.0) × 1.0 surge, the multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the SGD 0.80 platform fee); a refund of SGD 6.31, rounded up to SGD 6.35 — but that refund cannot issue while the only evidence of the deviation is an impaired trace that no independent source corroborates. I reject the driver's argument that the trip record's 18.2 km is independent corroboration: POL-RD-01 makes it a rounded convenience copy of the same trace measurement. I accept the remaining claims — no pickup/dropoff amendment (POL-RD-05), RYDE_X and not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12), an empty chat log leaving no rider-requested detour (POL-RD-04), no ERP or surcharge line to correct (POL-RD-09), and neither profile triggering the POL-RD-06 pattern or the POL-RD-08 corroboration test (POL-GEN-01) — but none of them changes the outcome.\n\nWhat would resolve it: an independent record of the route — a GPS export, an ERP gantry record placing the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use, or a driver admission of the route. The reviewer should ask for one of these; the escalation packet carries both advocate briefs and the admissibility report."
